1
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:04,450
Man, it's freezing.

2
00:00:05,010 --> 00:00:07,550
How long are they going
at it today? Jeez...

3
00:00:08,670 --> 00:00:12,370
I haven't eaten anything since
this morning. I'm starving.

4
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:16,030
What should I eat when I get home?

5
00:00:26,970 --> 00:00:30,310
Huh? But I told you bigger was better.

6
00:00:30,310 --> 00:00:33,000
If we're going to make it fight,
heavier is the best choice.

7
00:00:33,810 --> 00:00:36,480
Oh, then go find it and call back later.

8
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:39,830
Hmm? He's gone?

9
00:00:39,830 --> 00:00:40,970
Did he go somewhere?

10
00:00:41,770 --> 00:00:44,360
Man, what a pain. Bathroom break?

11
00:00:51,170 --> 00:00:52,920
Hey, look!

12
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:55,990
Think it eats fish sausage?

13
00:00:56,470 --> 00:00:59,010
Wait, that thing was in the
tournament, wasn't it?

14
00:00:59,550 --> 00:01:01,620
Here you go. It's fish sausage.

15
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:02,050
Come on, pandas don't meat, you know.

16
00:01:01,620 --> 00:01:02,700
It's tasty.

17
00:01:02,050 --> 00:01:03,450
It's bamboo. They eat bamboo.

18
00:01:04,070 --> 00:01:06,170
I'll take the fish sausage.

19
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:11,420
No cameras on the emergency stairs!

20
00:01:12,020 --> 00:01:13,070
Yo!

21
00:01:14,530 --> 00:01:17,380
Panda-senpai, are you really sure?

22
00:01:17,890 --> 00:01:20,100
This could cause you trouble later.

23
00:01:20,590 --> 00:01:22,690
It's fine, it's fine!

24
00:01:22,690 --> 00:01:25,010
Let's secure the area near the door.

25
00:01:35,730 --> 00:01:37,350
Gah! Kirara!

26
00:01:37,350 --> 00:01:39,380
Why isn't Kirara with Hakari?!

27
00:01:41,110 --> 00:01:42,550
Panda-chan?

28
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:45,750
And... that spiky-haired kid.

29
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:49,640
If Panda-chan helped him
sneak in here, that means...

30
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:51,470
he's with Jujutsu High?

31
00:01:51,470 --> 00:01:55,350
That means Yu-chan is
with Jujutsu High, too!

32
00:01:56,210 --> 00:01:59,320
Kin-chan's in danger!

33
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:01,660
Boss, I need to—

34
00:02:05,430 --> 00:02:07,600
Demon Dogs: Totality!

35
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:08,820
Hop!

36
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:17,020
Fushiguro?!

37
00:02:21,790 --> 00:02:24,070
My Demon Dog was thrown back?!

38
00:02:24,070 --> 00:02:28,440
No, judging from what Panda-senpai
said, it couldn't get close!

39
00:02:31,790 --> 00:02:34,540
I've already marked Panda-chan.

40
00:02:39,270 --> 00:02:40,900
The monitor room!

41
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:43,060
Kirara's planning to head back to Hakari!

42
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:44,560
Wait, Kirara!

43
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:46,110
We're not your enemies!

44
00:02:46,110 --> 00:02:48,360
We just want to ask Hakari for a favor!

45
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:49,750
I don't believe you!

46
00:02:49,750 --> 00:02:51,560
I'm disappointed in you, Panda-chan!

47
00:02:52,350 --> 00:02:55,820
Oh, I can't get close to you, either!

48
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:57,450
Ow!

49
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:01,680
So Kirara-san can't get
close to us, either?

50
00:03:03,710 --> 00:03:04,830
Fushiguro?!

51
00:03:04,830 --> 00:03:07,230
It's more than just being unable
to approach Kirara-san.

52
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:09,580
I can't separate from Demon Dogs, either?!

53
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:11,210
What kind of cursed technique is this?!

54
00:03:12,910 --> 00:03:14,020
Listen to me!

55
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:15,090
No way!

56
00:03:15,090 --> 00:03:16,760
My passion's gone cold now!

57
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:29,190
JUJUTSU KAISEN

58
00:03:52,460 --> 00:03:56,670
JUJUTSU KAISEN
The Culling Game Part 1

59
00:04:48,010 --> 00:04:51,010
Episode 53
Cog

60
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:57,330
We're in a stalemate.

61
00:04:57,330 --> 00:04:58,450
Perfect.

62
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:00,210
Kirara-san!

63
00:05:00,210 --> 00:05:03,330
We're not actually with
Jujutsu High right now!

64
00:05:03,330 --> 00:05:06,400
You know what Tokyo is
like now, don't you?

65
00:05:08,540 --> 00:05:11,500
The barriers that sprung up in
each region are related, too.

66
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:14,500
It was an unprecedented attack
of jujutsu terrorism!

67
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:17,000
We need Hakari-san's help!

68
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,640
You all are the ones
who excluded us first.

69
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:21,500
You reap what you sow.

70
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:23,600
I told you, we're not with Jujutsu High!

71
00:05:24,150 --> 00:05:26,030
What happened between
you and the higher-ups?

72
00:05:26,030 --> 00:05:28,130
They fought with the conservatives.

73
00:05:28,130 --> 00:05:33,520
Their idea of "conservative" goes beyond
just their policy toward the regulations.

74
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:37,270
They have set ideas of
what jujutsu should be.

75
00:05:37,510 --> 00:05:40,350
Kugisaki's technique is a good example.

76
00:05:40,350 --> 00:05:43,440
That's the kind of classic
jujutsu the conservatives like.

77
00:05:44,080 --> 00:05:46,830
Not stuff like the cursed videos
that were popular a while back.

78
00:05:46,830 --> 00:05:50,320
As time goes on, even jujutsu
incorporates more new technologies.

79
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:53,010
But when even techniques
start doing that,

80
00:05:53,010 --> 00:05:54,910
the conservatives get fussy.

81
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:58,640
Kin-chan's technique
is a perfect example.

82
00:05:58,640 --> 00:06:01,120
Those stupid higher-ups lost
because they're like that.

83
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:06,320
But you all can always have
Satoru Gojo wipe your asses, can't you?

84
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:09,150
I don't understand why
you need to rely on us.

85
00:06:09,150 --> 00:06:12,110
So obviously I'd assume that means
you're lying about relying on us,

86
00:06:12,110 --> 00:06:15,350
and you're here for
some other reason, right?

87
00:06:16,390 --> 00:06:18,690
Gojo-sensei was sealed.

88
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:20,670
That's why we lost.

89
00:06:34,820 --> 00:06:37,040
They don't believe us!

90
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:43,840
They don't believe us!

91
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:39,590
Well, I can understand that.

92
00:06:39,590 --> 00:06:43,490
But this person is the one
closest to Hakari-san!

93
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:44,840
Fleeing Hares!

94
00:06:46,080 --> 00:06:47,400
Bunnies?

95
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:49,120
If we can convince them,

96
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:51,520
negotiations with Hakari-san
will go more smoothly!

97
00:06:54,940 --> 00:06:56,100
Acrux?!

98
00:06:58,470 --> 00:07:00,000
Gacrux?!

99
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:02,540
What an incredible amount.

100
00:07:02,540 --> 00:07:04,140
What is he up to?

101
00:07:04,740 --> 00:07:08,070
My technique marks cursed energy,

102
00:07:08,350 --> 00:07:11,690
so it treats sorcerers and their
shikigami as one in the same.

103
00:07:11,690 --> 00:07:15,190
At this rate, they'll just be
drawn to him like that doggy was,

104
00:07:15,190 --> 00:07:18,170
and he'll be crushed under his own
shikigami until he suffocates.

105
00:07:29,630 --> 00:07:30,770
Panda-senpai!

106
00:07:30,770 --> 00:07:32,140
How was Fleeing Hares?!

107
00:07:32,590 --> 00:07:34,470
They were second to me in cuteness!

108
00:07:34,470 --> 00:07:38,140
I'm asking you what they were
and weren't able to approach!

109
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:39,580
Oh.

110
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:42,560
They were able to come to me and
that second floor no problem!

111
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:45,240
They couldn't get near Kirara and
the door to the monitor room!

112
00:07:45,870 --> 00:07:49,990
Panda-senpai, do you have a star
and a name somewhere on your body?

113
00:07:50,520 --> 00:07:51,460
Huh?

114
00:07:51,890 --> 00:07:52,900
Oh!

115
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:54,870
I-M-A-I?

116
00:07:54,870 --> 00:07:56,190
One should be somewhere on me...

117
00:07:56,190 --> 00:07:57,460
Ima? Ima? Imai?

118
00:07:57,390 --> 00:07:58,470
There!

119
00:07:57,460 --> 00:07:59,210
It says "Imai"!

120
00:07:59,210 --> 00:08:01,320
It's "Acrux," like on the Fleeing Hares!

121
00:08:01,780 --> 00:08:03,810
It's probably on Demon Dogs, too.

122
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:07,490
I still don't know anything
about it, but I should...

123
00:08:08,770 --> 00:08:10,100
I got it!

124
00:08:10,100 --> 00:08:12,370
This technique is based
on a constellation!

125
00:08:12,760 --> 00:08:15,390
People familiar with them
could figure that out.

126
00:08:15,390 --> 00:08:17,170
The constellation it's based on is...

127
00:08:22,020 --> 00:08:23,520
the Southern Cross!

128
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:30,070
Shit!

129
00:08:30,310 --> 00:08:32,720
We both let it show on our faces!

130
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:45,590
Seriously?

131
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:35,200
His look said, "Seriously?!"

132
00:08:35,550 --> 00:08:39,950
He wasn't certain my technique
was based on the Southern Cross!

133
00:08:39,950 --> 00:08:42,770
But I also gave him the same look!

134
00:08:42,770 --> 00:08:44,600
I confirmed it for him!

135
00:08:45,010 --> 00:08:47,260
If he figures out any
more of my technique,

136
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:49,000
he'll be able to enter the monitor room!

137
00:08:49,710 --> 00:08:51,960
I have to stop him here!

138
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:53,790
Back in a stalemate again?

139
00:08:56,220 --> 00:08:58,730
Still, it really was the Southern Cross?

140
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:01,510
I'm grateful to Tsumiki.

141
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:04,040
I don't know anything else, though.

142
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:07,040
Also, wasn't the Southern Cross
a four-star constellation?

143
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:08,650
Fushiguro!

144
00:09:09,190 --> 00:09:11,630
I really can get close to Panda-senpai.

145
00:09:12,540 --> 00:09:16,290
Senpai, the Southern Cross
has four stars, right?

146
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:16,920
Huh?

147
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:18,650
Well, it is a cross.

148
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:21,230
Yeah, I guess so.

149
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:30,790
Kirara-san's technique applies one of the
stars in the Southern Cross to each of us,

150
00:09:30,790 --> 00:09:34,030
and I thought it might use that to force
us to maintain a certain distance.

151
00:09:34,030 --> 00:09:36,860
But Kirara-san can approach the door,

152
00:09:36,860 --> 00:09:39,510
and you and I can approach each other.

153
00:09:39,510 --> 00:09:45,350
Maybe it's just that Kirara and the
door's stars are repelling ours?

154
00:09:41,890 --> 00:09:44,850
"Cross Theory"

155
00:09:45,660 --> 00:09:47,320
If that were true,

156
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:50,240
it would make more sense for Kirara-san
to flee into the monitor room.

157
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:51,630
Oh, true.

158
00:09:51,630 --> 00:09:54,770
If they hugged the inside of
the door, we'd be stuck.

159
00:09:55,750 --> 00:09:57,600
Then what about this?

160
00:09:58,130 --> 00:10:03,650
Star A is able to approach Star B,
but B can't approach A.

161
00:10:03,650 --> 00:10:06,750
Each Star has one they're compatible with,

162
00:10:06,750 --> 00:10:09,550
and they can only approach that one.

163
00:10:09,540 --> 00:10:11,380
"Rock-Paper-Scissors Theory"

164
00:10:09,550 --> 00:10:10,890
Like in rock-paper-scissors.

165
00:10:11,390 --> 00:10:16,550
But you and I can approach
each other and move freely.

166
00:10:16,890 --> 00:10:18,410
So that's not it, then.

167
00:10:20,550 --> 00:10:23,320
I think it's like a stamp rally,

168
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:26,320
where you have to follow a set route
and approach each one in order.

169
00:10:26,930 --> 00:10:29,210
And things with the same
star get drawn together.

170
00:10:28,770 --> 00:10:30,270
"Stamp Rally Theory"

171
00:10:30,260 --> 00:10:31,890
I see.

172
00:10:31,890 --> 00:10:35,360
But what if the sorcerer
isn't counted as a target?

173
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:37,000
That can't be the case.

174
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,540
They were forced to stay
away from Demon Dogs, too.

175
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:42,010
Right now, Kirara-san is wary

176
00:10:42,010 --> 00:10:44,110
of us fulfilling some kind of condition

177
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:49,800
out of their sight that's needed
to enter the monitor room.

178
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:53,240
Then there are five or more stars.

179
00:10:53,240 --> 00:10:53,930
Right.

180
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:57,380
If my stamp rally theory is correct,

181
00:10:57,380 --> 00:11:02,070
then we should be able to approach
Kirara-san if there are only four stars.

182
00:11:02,070 --> 00:11:04,440
So there has to be a fifth star

183
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:07,780
that we have to pass through in order
to reach Kirara-san and the door.

184
00:11:08,340 --> 00:11:10,720
What if there are six or seven stars?

185
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:13,470
I'd like to believe that's not the case.

186
00:11:13,470 --> 00:11:16,140
It's already confusing that there
would be five stars in a cross.

187
00:11:16,140 --> 00:11:17,150
If they've figured it out,

188
00:11:18,410 --> 00:11:19,390
then I have to attack!

189
00:11:27,910 --> 00:11:28,920
Panda-senpai!

190
00:11:31,130 --> 00:11:32,570
I'm okay!

191
00:11:32,570 --> 00:11:33,740
Don't worry about me!

192
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:36,770
Fushiguro! Find the star!

193
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:43,140
Hey! You can't throw it!

194
00:11:43,140 --> 00:11:44,050
Huh?

195
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:50,920
They put the same Imai star on that car!

196
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:52,540
If you throw it, it'll just come back

197
00:11:52,540 --> 00:11:55,240
or pull you toward it
like Demon Dogs did to me!

198
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:58,550
They probably have to touch
the target to plant a star.

199
00:11:59,050 --> 00:12:02,280
But Kirara-san hasn't touched
me or Fleeing Hares.

200
00:12:03,230 --> 00:12:05,000
She only touched Demon Dogs.

201
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:09,000
Meaning Kirara-san is tagging
cursed energy, not objects!

202
00:12:09,290 --> 00:12:12,070
In order to tag doors and cars,

203
00:12:12,070 --> 00:12:15,530
they should need someone to imbue cursed
energy into them ahead of time.

204
00:12:19,830 --> 00:12:20,960
I knew it!

205
00:12:22,140 --> 00:12:24,980
The car has residual cursed
energy from someone else!

206
00:12:25,440 --> 00:12:27,740
If the technique doesn't
cover a wide range,

207
00:12:27,740 --> 00:12:29,600
then traces of the other
star should be...

208
00:12:41,730 --> 00:12:42,580
There!

209
00:12:42,580 --> 00:12:44,000
The fifth star!

210
00:12:44,830 --> 00:12:48,200
I don't see any more residuals
from someone other than us.

211
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:51,330
Kirara-san's already marked
their own cursed energy,

212
00:12:51,330 --> 00:12:54,410
so they can't use their
own cursed energy

213
00:12:54,410 --> 00:12:56,470
to mark objects with the same
Acrux star they gave me.

214
00:12:56,470 --> 00:12:59,620
Meaning they can't launch things
at me like they did with that car!

215
00:13:01,130 --> 00:13:03,730
Once I touch that,
I can approach Kirara-san!

216
00:13:05,730 --> 00:13:08,060
Fushiguro's hypothesis was correct.

217
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:11,810
Kirara's cursed technique,
Love Rendezvous,

218
00:13:11,810 --> 00:13:17,730
apportions five stars to targets' cursed
energy with the Southern Cross as a base.

219
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:21,640
For one star to approach another,

220
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:24,480
it must follow a predetermined order,

221
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:28,120
and things marked with the
same star attract each other.

222
00:13:28,970 --> 00:13:30,630
You're incredible.

223
00:13:30,630 --> 00:13:33,490
You actually figured out my technique.

224
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:35,120
Panda-senpai!

225
00:13:49,570 --> 00:13:52,890
That order was nearest
to the farthest star.

226
00:13:53,350 --> 00:13:57,200
Constellations may look flat,
but they do, of course, have depth,

227
00:13:57,200 --> 00:14:00,470
and each star has a different
distance from Earth.

228
00:14:00,830 --> 00:14:02,150
But since you're too smart,

229
00:14:02,150 --> 00:14:05,910
you decided I could no longer
throw objects at you, didn't you?

230
00:14:05,910 --> 00:14:09,680
I can just lift the Ginan star
placed on my own cursed energy

231
00:14:09,680 --> 00:14:13,120
and mark things with the same
Acrux star that's on you!

232
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:21,670
What?!

233
00:14:22,550 --> 00:14:24,690
How?! Where did it come from?!

234
00:14:24,690 --> 00:14:26,540
No, that's it! That boy...

235
00:14:27,160 --> 00:14:30,670
never dismissed his doggy shikigami!

236
00:14:30,670 --> 00:14:31,870
Did he figure out which of

237
00:14:31,870 --> 00:14:34,180
the same tagged objects
would be drawn to the other?!

238
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:37,160
Then he put a wall between
himself and the shikigami

239
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:40,310
so the shikigami would
be drawn into the wall,

240
00:14:40,730 --> 00:14:44,260
and unleashed the doggy when
I was in a line between them!

241
00:14:45,100 --> 00:14:47,400
Love Rendezvous, cancel!

242
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:08,720
Please hear us out.

243
00:15:11,190 --> 00:15:13,980
JUJUTSU KAISEN

244
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:18,970
JUJUTSU KAISEN

245
00:15:22,390 --> 00:15:26,100
Did you really set that up on purpose?

246
00:15:26,100 --> 00:15:29,810
You couldn't have known if you or the
doggy would get pulled toward the other.

247
00:15:29,810 --> 00:15:32,460
I took a gamble, but now I'm certain.

248
00:15:32,870 --> 00:15:35,770
The one with greater cursed energy
pulls the other toward it, right?

249
00:15:36,570 --> 00:15:39,370
The first time, I was
pulled into Demon Dogs,

250
00:15:39,370 --> 00:15:43,320
but when I strengthened my cursed
energy to guard against your attack,

251
00:15:43,320 --> 00:15:44,960
the opposite happened.

252
00:15:45,690 --> 00:15:47,720
Are you really a first-year?

253
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:49,640
You really aren't cute at all.

254
00:15:54,430 --> 00:15:57,440
Please. We don't have time.

255
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:59,070
Please hear us out.

256
00:16:01,070 --> 00:16:02,550
Fine.

257
00:16:10,710 --> 00:16:12,050
Itadori?!

258
00:16:12,050 --> 00:16:14,320
Fushiguro, Panda-senpai...

259
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:16,750
Stay out of this!

260
00:16:28,990 --> 00:16:31,120
Underestimating me, huh?

261
00:16:33,130 --> 00:16:33,970
Straight to the face!

262
00:16:36,350 --> 00:16:39,100
This brat! He's not...

263
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:41,110
even trying to dodge!

264
00:16:41,110 --> 00:16:42,720
You're crazy.

265
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:46,370
This isn't like the fight in Shibuya.

266
00:16:46,780 --> 00:16:49,810
This is basically a ritual
to make Hakari-senpai

267
00:16:49,810 --> 00:16:51,360
acknowledge me.

268
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:53,640
I won't dodge anymore.

269
00:16:53,640 --> 00:16:55,250
I won't fight back.

270
00:16:57,160 --> 00:16:59,630
Not until he caves.

271
00:16:59,630 --> 00:17:02,620
Interesting! I'll listen to you...

272
00:17:03,090 --> 00:17:05,190
for as long as you remain standing!

273
00:17:05,190 --> 00:17:06,220
Kin-chan!

274
00:17:06,220 --> 00:17:08,830
These kids just want your help!

275
00:17:08,830 --> 00:17:10,830
Hear them out!

276
00:17:10,830 --> 00:17:12,870
I just said I would!

277
00:17:19,070 --> 00:17:22,980
So, Itadori, why me?

278
00:17:22,980 --> 00:17:25,390
This is the first time we've met, right?

279
00:17:25,870 --> 00:17:27,920
So why rely on me?

280
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:30,670
Because my senpai

281
00:17:30,670 --> 00:17:32,910
all said you're strong.

282
00:17:34,180 --> 00:17:36,240
Figures.

283
00:17:36,730 --> 00:17:39,320
Whenever a sorcerer asks
another sorcerer for help,

284
00:17:39,320 --> 00:17:42,780
it's understood they're asking
him to risk his life with them!

285
00:17:44,030 --> 00:17:48,960
So you have to show me you have
passion worth risking my life for!

286
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:52,680
Right here and now!

287
00:17:52,680 --> 00:17:57,180
Yet you're telling me you came
here on orders without that?

288
00:17:57,180 --> 00:17:59,130
What the hell was old man Yaga thinking?!

289
00:17:59,130 --> 00:18:01,180
He should be weeding out losers like you!

290
00:18:04,900 --> 00:18:06,680
I don't have any passion.

291
00:18:06,980 --> 00:18:07,630
Huh?

292
00:18:08,090 --> 00:18:09,650
I'm a cog.

293
00:18:10,490 --> 00:18:16,560
A cog in the machine that sorcerers
need to keep exorcising curses.

294
00:18:17,610 --> 00:18:20,290
Wait, wait, wait. Are you for real?

295
00:18:20,870 --> 00:18:23,120
That's super disappointing.

296
00:18:23,490 --> 00:18:25,500
This is bad! Itadori, that's enough!

297
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:42,780
Hurts, doesn't it?

298
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:44,800
According to Gojo-san,

299
00:18:45,370 --> 00:18:49,060
my cursed energy's coarser and
grittier than that of others.

300
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:53,540
You dead?

301
00:18:55,810 --> 00:18:57,220
Hey, Panda!

302
00:18:57,220 --> 00:18:58,890
Sea Urchin Head!

303
00:18:58,890 --> 00:19:02,640
Take Itadori and get lost already.
Don't come ba—

304
00:19:04,430 --> 00:19:05,430
Huh?!

305
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:09,680
He took three unguarded blows!

306
00:19:09,680 --> 00:19:11,500
And I punched him a
bunch before then, too!

307
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:14,260
What are you made of?

308
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:16,590
I'm a cog.

309
00:19:16,590 --> 00:19:18,680
Cogs have a function, you know.

310
00:19:19,780 --> 00:19:22,840
My function is to keep exorcising curses.

311
00:19:22,840 --> 00:19:25,860
If you're necessary to achieve that,

312
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:28,850
then I'll play along
until you agree to it.

313
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:43,790
Senpai.

314
00:19:44,760 --> 00:19:46,700
What is your function?

315
00:19:47,510 --> 00:19:48,780
This kid...

316
00:19:49,930 --> 00:19:52,410
So this is a cog's passion?

317
00:19:56,540 --> 00:19:58,830
Fine. I'll keep punching—

318
00:19:58,830 --> 00:20:00,040
Kin-chan.

319
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:02,650
He's gotten you heated up, hasn't he?

320
00:20:06,780 --> 00:20:09,380
Passion never lies.

321
00:20:13,190 --> 00:20:14,860
Get down here, you three.

322
00:20:14,860 --> 00:20:15,900
Huh?

323
00:20:16,700 --> 00:20:18,150
Let's cut a deal.

324
00:20:20,220 --> 00:20:22,460
Huh? It's resolved?

325
00:20:23,030 --> 00:20:25,250
Did you just convince him?

326
00:20:25,250 --> 00:20:26,130
Yeah.

327
00:20:26,130 --> 00:20:27,780
Thank you.

328
00:20:27,780 --> 00:20:28,720
Don't mention it.

329
00:20:29,180 --> 00:20:31,650
We may hate the upper brass,

330
00:20:31,650 --> 00:20:37,120
but Kin-chan always burned hottest when
he was helping others at Jujutsu High.

331
00:20:38,230 --> 00:20:38,910
Ow!

332
00:20:41,660 --> 00:20:45,640
Ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong,
ding-dong, ding-dong, ding-dong!

333
00:20:42,580 --> 00:20:43,530
What?!

334
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:52,010
A Player has added a new
rule to the Culling Game!

335
00:20:52,010 --> 00:20:55,900
Rule 9: Players shall be able to view the
following information on other players:

336
00:20:55,900 --> 00:21:02,440
name, points, number of
rules added, current Colony.

337
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:05,450
8: Players who do not show a
change in points within 19 days of
joining or acquiring points
shall be stripped of their technique.

338
00:21:05,450 --> 00:21:08,820
9: Players shall be able to view the
following information on other players:
name, points, number of
rules added, current Colony.

339
00:21:07,900 --> 00:21:10,340
You have gained five points.

340
00:21:10,830 --> 00:21:13,240
Damn right. I killed him.

341
00:21:16,940 --> 00:21:20,510
Every one of these guys is too weak.

342
00:21:20,510 --> 00:21:23,460
It was better 400 years ago.

343
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:28,020
Where are you, Sukuna?

344
00:21:32,810 --> 00:21:35,380
You have exceeded 200 points.

345
00:21:35,380 --> 00:21:40,010
Would you like to consume 100 points
to add a rule to the Culling Game?

346
00:21:40,630 --> 00:21:43,180
Right, the rules.

347
00:21:43,900 --> 00:21:48,260
If I knew their names, and points
would demonstrate their strength...

348
00:21:49,340 --> 00:21:52,650
Oh, but points go down
when adding a rule.

349
00:21:52,650 --> 00:21:55,250
So I'd need the number
of rules they added, too.

350
00:21:55,960 --> 00:21:58,860
And also which colony they're in.

351
00:21:59,570 --> 00:22:00,720
Kogane.

352
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:02,200
Add a rule.

353
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:05,080
Reveal that information for every player.

354
00:22:05,340 --> 00:22:08,800
Culling Game Player Hajime Kashimo

355
00:23:41,840 --> 00:23:43,930
You're in the space between
dreams and reality.

356
00:23:43,930 --> 00:23:45,060
It's a curse.

357
00:23:45,060 --> 00:23:46,660
How do you know my name?

358
00:23:46,660 --> 00:23:47,780
I'm not like Itadori.

359
00:23:47,780 --> 00:23:50,640
Once you step inside,
you, too, become a Player!

360
00:23:50,640 --> 00:23:53,720
...and make them add a rule to let
Tsumiki escape the Culling Game!

361
00:23:51,990 --> 00:23:55,110
Next Episode
Tokyo Colony No. 1
